    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0513" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg439"/>

                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 4, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to send you a despatch of
                    Dr. Williams marked A, with enclosures marked B and C, prepared to send through
                    Russia, but which was finally transmitted to me. This gives so clear a history
                    of the difficulty at Peking, that it is not necessary for me to do more than to
                    commend it to your careful perusal.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BURLINGAME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




